fact WorkItem(id: "WI-230", description: some(value: "Operation-call-model: convert requires_chain from flat Vec<RequiresEntry> to tree-structured Vec<RequireNode>. Follow-up to WI-226. Today the typer's requires_chain returns a flat transitive closure, while WI-223's RequirementHandle arena stores sub-handles as a tree. This asymmetry forces WI-227 to re-derive nesting via caller_sub_chains and joined-list lookups; the substitution chain (Wi222Outer.T → Ordered.T → Eq.T) is implicit and recovered at each use site. Scope: (a) introduce RequireNode { entry: RequiresEntry, sub_requires: Vec<RequireNode> } in kb/typing.rs; (b) rewrite collect_requires to produce a tree (each direct require carries its own sub-tree); (c) thread substitution composition through tree construction so each leaf carries fully-substituted bindings (Eq's T at Wi222Outer-scope = Wi222Outer.T directly, not Ordered.T); (d) migrate consumers: TypingEnv.requires field, build_dep_projection Strategy 2 (becomes tree-walk), candidate_sub_goals_owned, sort_refines, check_obligations, eval/mod.rs's seed_entry_requirements, op_requirements; (e) cache becomes Rc<RequireNode> with natural sub-tree sharing — Ordered's sub-tree is the same instance whether reached via Wi222Outer or Wi222Multi; (f) the cycle-corruption issue from WI-226's flat-cache discussion disappears because back-edges become a CycleBack node variant or simply aren't added, not a truncated list. Acceptance: cargo-test green; all WI-222/WI-223/WI-224/WI-227/WI-228 tests pass with the new tree representation; new test pins (1) tree shape matches the declared requires hierarchy for a 3-level chain; (2) substitution composition: Eq's leaf in Wi222Outer's tree carries T = Wi222Outer.T (not Ordered.T); (3) shared sub-tree identity: requires_tree(Wi222Multi) and requires_tree(Wi222Outer) reference the same Rc when both transitively requires Ordered. Out of scope: changing the runtime arena (already tree-shaped). Reference: docs/design/operation-call-model.md §'Runtime: frame, requirement value, closure' (RequirementSlot is already tree-shaped at runtime — this WI brings typer-side in line)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-226"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-12T05:26:44Z"))
